From 25e67964d8238ef9cd514acac34919052dbc80fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 13:40:21 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(skills): optimize + triggering-test descriptions and add
 evals for all 18 skills
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Brings the whole skill library to the skill-creator standard on its primary
axis — triggering. For each of the 18 skills, rewrites the frontmatter
description to be pushy (Claude under-triggers) and explicitly discriminating
against sibling skills so a query routes to exactly one, and adds an
evals/evals.json trigger set (realistic should_trigger queries + near-miss
should_not-trigger queries drawn from sibling territory).

Produced by a 3-stage multi-agent pass: audit (verify every cited forge/CLI
flag against live --help) -> adversarial verify (independently re-check routing
and accuracy) -> blind routing test (a judge predicts fire/no-fire over the full
optimized description set with the answer key hidden; scored deterministically).
All 18 skills scored 100% trigger pass-rate with 0 misroutes.

Bodies are byte-identical (only the frontmatter description block changed);
.codex mirror regenerated (checkSkillsSync inSync). A separate follow-up will
correct CLI-command inaccuracies found in some skill BODIES (the body-fix set
had cross-skill contradictions and Beads-vs-kernel issues that need ground-truth
verification, so it is intentionally not bundled here).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
